        <p>Repealed by ORD C34438.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 8, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 16, 2009</p><p>ORD C34438 Section 1</p>				<p></p>
        				<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.23A">Chapter 10.23A</a> Amusement Facilities</p>
        					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.010">Section 10.23A.010</a> Definitions<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">For the purpose of this chapter:</span></span></p>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;All ages venue&rdquo; is an entertainment facility where live or recorded entertainment involving music, singing, dancing, or other similar entertainment is presented to the public, where patrons of all ages are admitted.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Amusement facility,&rdquo; or &ldquo;entertainment facility&rdquo; is any business, club, or location that is required to have a City business license or permit in accordance with&nbsp;<a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=08.01">chapter </a></span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=08.01"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">08.01</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> SMC&nbsp;where concerts, dances, carnivals, circuses, teen club, all ages venue, or a cabaret is presented to the public as a regular course of doing business, not including:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">a government entity, public or private schools or college; or</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">a facility operated by an organization which has been recognized as exempt from federal income taxation and when the entertainment activities are but an occasional activity not related to the facility&rsquo;s primary purposes; or</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">licensed businesses whose primary function is to provide products or services and where the entertainment provided is not material to the economic viability of the business.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Cabaret&rdquo; is an entertainment venue involving live or recorded music, singing, dancing, or other similar entertainment that is presented to the public.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Carnivals&rdquo; are any organized event for the primary purpose of presenting a traveling show having sideshows, rides, games of skill, and food vendors, whether indoors or outdoors.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Circuses&rdquo; are any organized event for the primary purpose of exhibition of feats of performers, entertainers, acrobats, and trained animals, whether indoors or outdoors.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Concerts&rdquo; are any organized event for the primary purpose of presenting live or recorded music or other amplified sounds for entertainment, whether indoors or outdoors.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Dance&rdquo; is any organized event for the primary purpose of presenting live or recorded music for dancing, whether indoors or outdoors.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Event facility&rdquo; is any establishment, licensed under this chapter, where an admission fee is charged and/or tickets are sold for entry which is being presented to the public.&rdquo;</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-roman">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Outdoor entertainment&rdquo; is a venue involving live or recorded music, singing, or other similar entertainment that is presented to the public.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="10" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Teen club&rdquo; is any building, or part of, or other enclosed facility, or place where a teen dance or venue is held or teen dancing is permitted.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="11" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Teen dance&rdquo; is a dance or venue open to the public to which persons under the age of twenty-one years are admitted.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="12" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&ldquo;Venue&rdquo; is an entertainment facility involving live or recorded music, singing, dancing, or other similar entertainment presented at a facility, location, or established place of business licensed under this chapter.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 1</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.020">Section 10.23A.020</a> License Required<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">No person may conduct or maintain an entertainment or amusement facility without first obtaining an entertainment facility license.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Anyone conducting or operating a business, event, or venue where concerts, dances, carnivals, or circuses are presented to the public as a regular course of doing business shall have a license or permit issued under this chapter, unless otherwise exempted by this chapter.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.030">Section 10.23A.030</a> Special Regulations for Entertainment Facilities<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No person under the age of eighteen years may be in a premise licensed under this section between the hours of two a.m. and six a.m., nor shall any licensee permit such minor to be on the premises between those hours.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No licensee may conduct any dancing activity between the hours of two a.m. and six a.m. without prior special permission of the license officer.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">The operator of an entertainment facility:</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">shall not permit music to emanate off the premises in violation of </span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=10.70">SMC 10.70</a><span style="color:black">, except where outdoor entertainment venues are provided in approved outdoor patio areas;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">shall ensure the subject premises comply with all applicable building, fire, and zoning codes; and</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Outdoor entertainment venues may be provided in approved outdoor patio areas pursuant to the following:</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Sound levels shall be in compliance with </span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=10.70">SMC 10.70</a><span style="color:black">.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">Sound levels must be turned down or terminated in response to neighborhood complaints or as directed by a police officer.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="margin-left:40px">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"><span style="color:black">No outdoor entertainment allowed after ten p.m., provided that, at the time of the initial permit application, a venue may request and shall receive a permit allowing for extended hours to midnight on Friday and Saturday if the venue is located no closer than one hundred feet from a residential zone, which shall be measured from the property lines between the venue and the nearest residential property.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li><span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="background-color:white"><span style="font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><span style="font-size:12.0pt"><span style="color:black">A violation under this section is a class one civil infraction for each violation.</span></span></span></span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 24, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, August 2, 2024</p><p>ORD C36528 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.040">Section 10.23A.040</a> REPEALED (Special Regulations for All-ages Venue)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 24, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, August 2, 2024</p><p>ORD C36528 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.050">Section 10.23A.050</a> Special Regulations for Circuses, Carnivals, Concerts, and Dances <br />
        <ol type="A">
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			An applicant for a permit under this section must make application at least thirty days prior to the date of the proposed event.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The applicant must demonstrate that no principal, manager, or person having a proprietary interest in the event has a criminal history related to such person&rsquo;s fitness to conduct the event, including specifically crimes of moral turpitude.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			If the event requires any special physical facilities, the applicant must furnish specific plans with the application.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The applicant must show the character, number, and location of all potable water and other drinking, food, toilet, lavatory, waste collection, and emergency medical facilities available and to be provided.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The applicant must show plans for traffic and crowd control by commissioned City police officers at the ratio of one traffic-control officer and one crowd-control officer for every two hundred persons expected to attend.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			The applicant must state the procedure to be used to limit further attendance in the event attendance exceeds the capacity of the approved physical, sanitation, or law enforcement facilities.</p>
        	</li>
        	<li>
        		<p>
        			Expiration and Transfer.<br />
        			The permit under this section is issued to a particular sponsor for a single event. The permit expires upon conclusion of the event and is not transferable. Unless otherwise determined by the license officer, the licensee must have the physical facilities provided for a circus, carnival, concert, or dance in place and ready for inspection by all interested officials five days prior to the event. A license issued under this section is not subject to the requirements listed elsewhere in this chapter.</p>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 5, 2017</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, July 19, 2017</p><p>ORD C35500 Section 6</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.060">Section 10.23A.060</a> REPEALED (Special Regulations for Teen Club)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 24, 2024</p><p>Effective Date: Friday, August 2, 2024</p><p>ORD C36528 Section 5</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.070">Section 10.23A.070</a> Application, Transfer, and Renewal<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An entertainment facility license issued under this chapter is not transferable as to person or place.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Application for License.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The application is filed and all applicable license fee(s) are paid to, the Taxes and Licensing Office.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The license officer, does not approve the license until the application has been reviewed and approved by a designated building official, fire marshal, and director of taxes and licenses as required.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An entertainment facility shall be at all times during normal business hours available for access by any law enforcement.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">This chapter is subject to the administrative provisions of&nbsp;chapter 08.01 SMC.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">An entertainment facility license may be suspended, revoked, or denied if:</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">any datum furnished on the application is false or is not updated in a timely fashion;</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="2" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">the structure ceases to comply with all applicable building, fire, and zoning provisions;</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="3" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">any condition of the license, or voluntary consent agreement issued under this chapter has been violated; or</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="list-style-type:none">
        		<ol start="4" style="list-style-type:lower-alpha">
        			<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">any provision of this chapter is violated.</span></span></li>
        		</ol>
        		</li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any authorized City official may issue a warning order requiring licensee to correct any condition or practice that presents a threat to the public health or safety.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Authorized City departments may invoke their powers granted under the Spokane Municipal Code to immediately close an entertainment facility if the conditions present an imminent threat to public health and safety.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="5" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Renewal of application:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Application for renewal shall be made no later than thirty days prior to expiration of license.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The applicant shall pay all applicable fees.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The applicant must obtain relevant confirmations from the fire department; the building services department; and the police department.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="6" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All license fees are non refundable.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="7" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any person required to obtain a license under this chapter and who fails to do so in the time required by this code is subject to payment of interest on the outstanding balance at the rate of one percent per month or part of a month. In addition to the interest, penalties are assessed at the rate of:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Fifteen percent for the amount due for any amount past due more than thirty days; and</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Twenty percent for the amount past due more than sixty days.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="8" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Penalties and interest provided for in this section are collected as part of the license fee. Collection of the penalties and interest, or discontinuance of the activity, does not excuse noncompliance and is not a defense to prosecution.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify">&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 3</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.075">Section 10.23A.075</a> REPEALED (Appeal of License Denial, Suspension or Revocation)<br />
        <p>REPEALED&nbsp;</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 4</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.080">Section 10.23A.080</a> Control over Adjacent Areas<br />
        <p>The licensee of an entertainment license is responsible and expected to exercise appropriate control over its customers, not only inside their establishment but also within the immediate vicinity for such purposes as preventing unnecessary noise, litter, trespass and property damage, traffic obstruction, and similar activities which may constitute a public or private nuisance to the detriment of the neighboring community.</p>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 8, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 16, 2009</p><p>ORD C34438 Section 2</p>					<a href="/smc/?Section=10.23A.090">Section 10.23A.090</a> Hold Harmless Agreement<br />
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">All persons applying for and holding permits/licenses issued under this chapter shall agree to the following as a condition of the permit/license:</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Indemnification.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p style="margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in; text-align:justify"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The licensee shall indemnify and hold the City of Spokane harmless from any and all losses, claims, actions or damages suffered by any person or persons by reason of or resulting from any negligence of the licensee or its agents, employees, or patrons or on account of any act or omission of the licensee in its exercise of its license or use or occupancy of any premises in connection with such license. In the event any suit or action is brought against the City, the licensee shall upon notice of commencement thereof, defend the same at no cost and expense to the City, and promptly satisfy any final judgment adverse to the City or to the City and the licensee.</span></span></span></p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, June 8, 2009</p><p>Effective Date: Thursday, July 16, 2009</p><p>ORD C34438 Section 2</p>				<p>Division II. License Code</p>
        						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.24A">Chapter 10.24A</a> REPEALED (Animal Control)</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.010">Section 10.24A.010</a> REPEALED (Potentially Dangerous Wild Animal)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.020">Section 10.24A.020</a> REPEALED (Enforcement — Law enforcement agencies and animal care and control agencies)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.030">Section 10.24A.030</a> REPEALED (Transporting or confining in unsafe manner — Penalty)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.040">Section 10.24A.040</a> REPEALED (Removal of animals for feeding and care — Examination — Notice — Euthanasia)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.050">Section 10.24A.050</a> REPEALED (Confinement without food and water — Intervention by others)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.060">Section 10.24A.060</a> REPEALED (Poisoning animals — Penalty)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.070">Section 10.24A.070</a> REPEALED (Sentences — Forfeiture of animals — Liability for costs — Penalty — Education, counseling)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.080">Section 10.24A.080</a> REPEALED (Animal cruelty in the second degree — Penalty)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.090">Section 10.24A.090</a> REPEALED (Dog breeding — Limit on the number of dogs — Required conditions — Penalty — Limitation of section — Definitions)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.100">Section 10.24A.100</a> REPEALED (When deemed abandoned)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.110">Section 10.24A.110</a> REPEALED (Disposition of abandoned animal by person having custody)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.120">Section 10.24A.120</a> REPEALED (Dangerous Wild Animals)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.130">Section 10.24A.130</a> REPEALED (Adoption of Revised Code of Washington by Reference)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.140">Section 10.24A.140</a> REPEALED (Animal Left in Vehicle or Enclosed Space)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.24A.150">Section 10.24A.150</a> REPEALED (Dog Tether Safety Standards)<br />
        <p>REPEALED</p>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>Effective Date: Monday, September 25, 2023</p><p>ORD C36445 Section 5</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.25">Chapter 10.25</a> Commercial Tree Work</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.25.010">Section 10.25.010</a> Commercial Tree License<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Any person or entity retained or hired to prune, plant, or remove a public tree or street tree as defined in <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=12.02.910"><span style="color:#0000ff">SMC 12.02.910</span></a> must be licensed to perform commercial tree work by the City under this section. Each day of a continuing violation is a new and separate violation. (Cross Reference: </span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=12.02.910" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 12.02.910</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">, et seq., pruning permit)</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A license to perform commercial tree work is issued to each applicant who meets the following qualifications:</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Is, or has an employee who is, an arborist certified through the International Society of Arboriculture.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Uses only International Society of Arboriculture certified arborist or certified tree workers in performing work which involves tree climbing or tree pruning, planting, or removal.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Has not been found in violation of any requirements of&nbsp;</span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=12.02" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">chapter 12.02</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> SMC&nbsp;within the preceding year.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Maintains public liability insurance with combined bodily injury and property damage limits of at least one million dollars. At the time of permit application, the applicant must furnish proof of such insurance, naming the City of Spokane as an additional insured. The insurance must include a provision for at least thirty days written notice to the City risk manager prior to cancellation or material change in coverage to be given. The risk manager may allow insurance to be provided on an annual basis and may increase the amount of coverage for more extensive work as the public interest may require.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The license expires one year from the date of issuance, or sooner if the liability insurance lapses.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="4" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Enforcement.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol>
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Whenever it appears to the City that there has been a violation of the Spokane Municipal Code by a licensee in connection with the enjoyment of licensed privileges, a warning letter is issued specifying the apparent violation and any other information. If the City believes damages apply, the warning letter may include that information and demand for payment. The letter shall state a time for response and offer to meet with the party. The City may always independently seek restitution for any damages through any lawful means.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="2">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If it appears to the City that a second violation has arisen within a three-year period after the first warning letter under subsection (E)(1) of this section, the matter is referred to the City prosecutor to seek penalties and full restitution for any apparent violations and damages claimed, including any items not resolved from the first warning letter. In addition, upon a court determination of any violation by a party required to hold a license under&nbsp;</span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.25.010" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 10.25.010</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">, said party&rsquo;s license is suspended six months. A party may apply for reinstatement after that time, conditioned on payment of all fines, penalties and damages applicable.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="3">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">If it appears to the City that a third violation has arisen within a three-year period after the first warning letter under subsection (E)(1) of this section, the matter is referred to the City prosecutor to seek penalties and full restitution for any apparent violations and damages claimed, including any items not resolved from prior accrued violations. In addition, upon a court determination of an additional violation by a party required to hold a license under&nbsp;</span><a href="http://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=10.25.010" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 10.25.010</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;beyond any prior court determination under subsection (E)(2) of this section, said party&rsquo;s license is suspended two years. A party may apply for reinstatement after that time, conditioned on payment of all fines, penalties and damages applicable.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol>
        	<li style="list-style-type:none">
        	<ol start="4">
        		<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Nothing herein prevents the City from contacting a party and resolving issues by any means outside the procedures stated herein.</span></span></li>
        	</ol>
        	</li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 5</p>						<p><a href="/smc/?Chapter=10.26">Chapter 10.26</a> Building Moving and Relocation</p>
        							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.26.010">Section 10.26.010</a> Relocation Permit Required<br />
        <ol style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">A person needs a relocation permit issued by the Development Services Center to relocate or place a building or structure upon any property in the city.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="2" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The applicant must be either the owner of the building or a state-registered contractor.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <ol start="3" style="list-style-type:upper-alpha">
        	<li style="text-align:justify"><span style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">The relocation permit is in addition to the building moving permit and the street obstruction permit as provided in&nbsp;</span><a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Section=17G.010.210" style="color:blue; text-decoration:underline" target="_blank"><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">SMC 17G.010.210(</span></a><span style="font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">B) and (D)&nbsp;and <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/?Chapter=12.02"><span style="color:#0000ff"><u>chapter&nbsp;12.02</u></span> </a>SMC. The relocation permit is a species of building permit.</span></span></li>
        </ol>
        
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, March 31, 2025</p><p>Effective Date: Saturday, May 10, 2025</p><p>ORD C36652 Section 6</p>							<a href="/smc/?Section=10.26.020">Section 10.26.020</a> Condition of Building <br />
        <ol type="A">
        <li>
        <p>The building official inspects the building to determine whether it complies with the current building code.</p></li>
        <li>If the building does not meet current code, the building official either denies the relocation permit application or conditions the permit on rehabilitation, repair or alteration. </li></ol>
        <blockquote>
        <p>All work of rehabilitation, repair or alteration required by a relocation permit is subject to the normal permit requirements of <a href="https://my.spokanecity.org/smc/" target="_blank">Title 17 SMC </a></p></blockquote>
        <p>Date Passed: Monday, January 11, 2016</p><p>Effective Date: Wednesday, February 24, 2016</p><p>ORD C35344 Section 2</p></form>
        </div>
        </div></td>
        	</tr>
        </table>
